{"id":"H5992","lemma":"עַמִּינָדָב","transliteration":"amminadav","sayIt":"am-mi-na-DAV","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Amminadab","meaning":"A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Exo.6.23;\nson of: Ram (H7410);\nfather of: Elisheba (H0472) and Nahshon (H5177)\nAlso named: Aminadab (Ἀμιναδάβ \"Amminadab\" G0284)\n§ Amminadab = \"my kinsman is noble\"\n1) son of Ram or Aram and father of Nahshon or Naasson and an ancestor of Jesus; father-in-law of Aaron\n2) a Kohathite Levite and chief of the sons of Uzziel\n3) a Levite, son of Kohath; also 'Izhar'","glosses":["amminadab"],"count":12,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"exo-6","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Amminadab","kjv":"of Amminadab"}},{"chapterId":"num-1","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Amminadab"}},{"chapterId":"num-2","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Amminadab","kjv":"of Amminadab"}},{"chapterId":"num-7","v":12,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Amminadab","kjv":"of Amminadab"}},{"chapterId":"num-7","v":17,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Amminadab"}},{"chapterId":"num-10","v":14,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Amminadab"}},{"chapterId":"rut-4","v":19,"renderings":{"bsb":"Amminadab"}},{"chapterId":"rut-4","v":20,"renderings":{"bsb":"Amminadab","kjv":"And Amminadab"}},{"chapterId":"1ch-2","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"Amminadab","kjv":"Amminadab"}},{"chapterId":"1ch-6","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"Amminadab","kjv":"Amminadab"}},{"chapterId":"1ch-15","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"Amminadab","kjv":"Amminadab"}},{"chapterId":"1ch-15","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"and Amminadab","kjv":"and Amminadab"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Exodus 6:23","note":"Aaron took Elisheba, the daughter of Amminadab, the sister of Nahshon, as his wife; and she bore him Nadab and Abihu, Eleazar and Ithamar.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Numbers 1:7","note":"Of Judah: Nahshon the son of Amminadab.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Ruth 4:19","note":"and Hezron became the father of Ram, and Ram became the father of Amminadab,","source":"web"},{"ref":"1 Chronicles 2:10","note":"Ram became the father of Amminadab, and Amminadab became the father of Nahshon, prince of the children of Judah;","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H3324","lemma":"יִצְהָר","transliteration":"yitshar","gloss":"Izhar"},{"id":"H0472","lemma":"אֱלִישֶׁ֫בַע","transliteration":"elisheva","gloss":"Elisheba"},{"id":"H5177","lemma":"נַחְשׁוֹן","transliteration":"nachshon","gloss":"Nahshon"},{"id":"H7410","lemma":"רָם","transliteration":"ram","gloss":"Ram"},{"id":"G0284","lemma":"Ἀμιναδάβ","transliteration":"aminadab","gloss":"Amminadab"},{"id":"H6955","lemma":"קְהָת","transliteration":"qehat","gloss":"Kohath"},{"id":"H6019","lemma":"עַמְרָם","transliteration":"amram","gloss":"Amram"},{"id":"H2275","lemma":"חֶבְרוֹן","transliteration":"chevron","gloss":"Hebron"}],"senses":[{"id":"H5992H","gloss":"Amminadab","relation":"H5992H ="},{"id":"H5992I","gloss":"Izhar","relation":"H5992I = a Name of"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}